  "generated_text": "1. The smallest four-digit number greater than 2999 is 3000.\n2. The middle two digits are 0 and 0.\n3. The product of 0 and 0 is 0, which does not exceed 5.\n4. Therefore, 3000 is not a valid number.\n5. The next four-digit number greater than 2999 is 3001.\n6. The middle two digits are 0 and 1.\n7. The product of 0 and 1 is 0, which does not exceed 5.\n8. Therefore, 3001 is not a valid number.\n9. The next four-digit number greater than 2999 is 3002.\n10. The middle two digits are 0 and 2.\n11. The product of 0 and 2 is 0, which does not exceed 5.\n12. Therefore, 3002 is not a valid number.\n\nThus, there are no four-digit numbers greater than 2999 that satisfy the given condition.\n\n\\boxed{0}",
